{"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"GnustoTestSupport","title":"GnustoTestSupport","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","modules":[{"name":"GnustoTestSupport"}]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"],"title":"Playing a session","anchor":"Playing-a-session"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(after:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)"],"title":"Slicing a transcript","anchor":"Slicing-a-transcript"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"],"title":"Asserting","anchor":"Asserting"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"],"anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","title":"Trapping a `fatalError`"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/frame(headed:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(ofLast:in:)"],"anchor":"Functions","generated":true,"title":"Functions"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is a value and a play session is a function of its typed input, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the natural test is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"transcript test","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" boots","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns everything printed with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"input interleaved as ","type":"text"},{"code":"> command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the same text the player saw. Everything else","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in this library either cuts that string down to the part a claim is about, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records a Swift Testing issue with the whole of it attached, which is what a bare","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"#expect(transcript.contains(…))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot do. Gnusto’s own suite is roughly a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"thousand tests of this shape.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is neither a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" bundle nor a ","type":"text"},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". It declares no verbs,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no rules and no entities, and a game never links it: it is a test-only helper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"library, and it imports the toolchain’s Testing library, which ships with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compiler rather than the OS. Put it in a test target’s dependencies and nowhere","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else — an executable that links it can fail at load time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The host passes a game type and a list of commands; the library holds one piece","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of state of its own, a process-wide cache of prepared games behind a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" exists because ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bootstrap.build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reflects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the game and every content bundle it lists, and that runs about 15× longer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a turn does. The suite boots the same handful of game types thousands of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"times, so building each once and copying the prepared definition takes bootstrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out of the suite’s critical path. ","type":"text"},{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" goes through it; a test that wants the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world rather than the transcript can call it directly and drive ","type":"text"},{"code":"REPL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" itself.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Gnusto catalog’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Testing Your Game","type":"text"}]},{"text":" article teaches four of these helpers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the habits around them — pinning a seed, sweeping ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_SEED"},{"text":" for tests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that pass by luck, deciding when a trap is worth a test at all. This page is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"list it stops short of.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"A transcript test","anchor":"A-transcript-test","type":"heading","level":2},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","@Test func ringingTheBellWinsTheGame() async throws {","    let transcript = try await play(","        MyGame(),","        [\"take rope\", \"north\", \"ring bell\"],","        seed: 7)","","    expectInOrder(","        transcript,","        [","            \"Village Garden\",","            \"Taken.\",","            \"Bell Tower\",","            \"The great bronze bell peals\",","        ])","","    let looking = turnOutput(of: \"examine hook\", in: transcript)","    #expect(looking.contains(\"screwed to the wall\"))","    #expect(occurrences(of: \"The bell tolls\", in: transcript) == 1)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Omit ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seed:"},{"text":" and the stream is fresh each run, unless ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_SEED"},{"text":" is set,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which pins every call that passed no seed of its own and leaves the ones that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"did alone. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"saveDirectory:"},{"text":" when a test exercises named ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"save"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"restore"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so it never writes to the real per-user saves directory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Slicing before asserting","anchor":"Slicing-before-asserting","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turnOutput(of:in:)"},{"text":" matches the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}]},{"text":" occurrence of a command, so a route","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that types ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"text":" four times wants four different commands or a different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"helper. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(after:in:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(before:in:)"},{"text":" cut on any marker rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a prompt, which is the slice for “and then, later…”. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"occurrences(of:in:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the count assertion — a beat that must fire exactly once.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lines(mentioning:in:)"},{"text":" returns the matching lines in transcript order, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what an alignment check compares between two runs to prove that a guard burned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"no randomness.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Asserting","anchor":"Asserting","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"text":" is the workhorse: a sequence of substrings, each match resuming","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"after the last, strict enough to pin the beats that matter and loose enough to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"survive an edit between them. The rest of the assertions are about a whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transcript rather than a phrase in it. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectEveryNounAnswered"},{"text":" fails on either","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"answer a game gives a noun it doesn’t know — ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I don't know the word \"x\""},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't see any such thing"},{"text":" — which is what a walk of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x <noun>"},{"text":" over a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"room’s own description is checking. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoAmbiguity"},{"text":" fails on ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which do you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mean…","type":"text"}]},{"text":", and is deliberately a separate call: an unanswered noun is always a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"defect, while an ambiguity is only one where the author believed the room held a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"single thing of that kind.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives"},{"text":" is for a game that has re-voiced the stub verbs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and wants to keep the claim whole. It reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Mirror"},{"text":" rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than naming the properties, so a stub added to the engine tomorrow is compared","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the day it lands. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"engineVoicedStubLines"},{"text":" is the same sweep without the issue","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recording, split out so the sweep itself can be tested for being alive — a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reflection loop that matches nothing passes silently.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Trapping a `fatalError`","anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine answers an authoring mistake by crashing with a message that names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it in a child process and read what it printed; Swift Testing’s exit tests do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the running and ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does the reading.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(MyGame(), [\"prime the bomb\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"names a daemon\", \"use startDaemon(_:)\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call is a child process, some 60 ms against 1 ms for an in-process","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertion, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"#expect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" has to stay at the call site because its body is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compiled into a C function that captures nothing. ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s own doc comment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"carries the rule for when that is worth spending, since it is where the person"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"deciding is standing: make the bad message unrepresentable and write no test,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"or split the message into a pure function and assert it in a millisecond, before","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"reaching for the third shape. Exit tests are built on macOS, Linux and Windows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and are absent elsewhere, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is compiled under "},{"code":"GNUSTO_EXIT_TESTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and a test using it wants a ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a suite that also runs on iOS, watchOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tvOS, visionOS or WASI.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/output(afterLast:in:)":{"type":"topic","title":"output(afterLast:in:)","abstract":[{"text":"Everything a transcript printed after its ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"last","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" occurrence of ","type":"text"},{"code":"marker","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/output(afterlast:in:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"output","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"afterLast","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS",